{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1209500-company-contracts-alternative-oaths","id":1209500,"title":"Company Contracts - alternative Oaths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-04-20T20:36:43-07:00","id":1209500,"title":"Company Contracts - alternative Oaths","content":"I\u2019m on an 11-hour layover and I wrote a thing: Company Contracts. They are alternatives to Invictus Oaths. A little less one-sided, a little more versatile and (I hope) a little more interesting.<br /> <br /> Doc: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1206jE5fLfqmr9z7ZJP2TbJLPBk1LPxpzekQk9c5LsMI\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...xpzekQk9c5LsMI</a><br /> <br /> The Company is an off-shoot of the Invictus. I was scribbling pirate vamp related things and then these guys happened. Not actually pirates, but boats are involved, historically at least:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Early in the 17th century business savvy Invictus from Amsterdam founded the Company. The organisation was explicitly modeled after the VOC, the Dutch East India Company, down to its stated mission goal: to profit from a monopolized overseas trade. Leeching off the resources and profits of its mortal counterpart was simple enough, the next step less so. It required encouraging all those European kindred who wished to migrate to new and distant worlds to enlist the services of the Company. By the end of the 1600s, the Company had done just that. At the cost of uncountable lives, both mortal and undead, it created for its ships and crews the reputation of least likely to end up in Davy Jones\u2019 locker. The success of the organisation allowed the faction a steady growth in power and slowly but surely it would come to completely consume its parent covenant from the inside out. <br /> <br /> -<br /> <br /> Tonight, its primary focus is still on the logistical side of commerce. But the covenant has kept up with the times, diversifying its spheres of influence to include all aspects of the market, from transport to the stock exchange, from banking systems to commodity industries. Company members maintain close relations with mortals. It\u2019s simply better for business. They believe, and not unreasonably so, that as long as you are filthy rich, you can pay your way out of most problematic situations you\u2019ll encounter in this world. That includes the nightly struggle of finding some bloody sustenance.<br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Would love some input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T21:06:59-07:00","id":1209885,"title":"","content":"I like these better than the Invictus oaths but their activation can get expensive. I imagine though that \u201ctechnically\u201d such arrangements could be similarly struck using oaths with the oath vassal dictating the terms and simply filling in the blanks during the swearing. But as they\u2019re written up, I really don\u2019t see much incentive for an Invictus to agree to taking a vassal for most of them. There\u2019s an unspoken implication in the title itself that the notary would act as a sort of harpy who would destroy the city status and reputation of either party but there\u2019s nothing explicit indicating that or empowering them in some kind of official or supernatural capacity like Carthian Laws have. <br /> <br /> I think your loan portion should be retooled. Loans usually involve borrowing something (possibly offering up collateral) and then paying the loan back in full with interest. With the way you have it written it basically looks like the client becomes a servant to the contractor with their payment for services being whatever \u201cloan\u201d they ask for.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s some questions on some of the mechanical aspects.<br /> <br /> Can you participate in multiple contracts at once? If yes, what happens if conflicting terms of different contracts arise?<br /> <br /> Does physically destroying a contract void it without the other drawbacks? (Other than the loss of blood.)<br /> <br /> What if both parties agree to end the contract before it\u2019s expiration?<br /> <br /> Which dice pool is used when a client uses the contractor to cast a specific ritual? It might be possible for someone to have a better dice pool than the contractor, they simply don\u2019t know the ritual in question. Alternatively hiring them to cast a specific spell may be pointless in the first place if they have to use their dice roll with nonproficiency penalties and don\u2019t have the attendant ranks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T03:27:40-07:00","id":1210881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1209500-company-contracts-alternative-oaths?p=1209885#post1209885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like these better than the Invictus oaths but their activation can get expensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>8 Vitae is the max at the moment, for a BPxMonths long faustian deal. I thought it was reasonable, but perhaps I don't see Vitae as a scarce enough resource?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I imagine though that \u201ctechnically\u201d such arrangements could be similarly struck using oaths with the oath vassal dictating the terms and simply filling in the blanks during the swearing. But as they\u2019re written up, I really don\u2019t see much incentive for an Invictus to agree to taking a vassal for most of them. </div> </div> </div>They could, I guess. But what I don't like about Oaths is their one-sidedness. Only one character invests Experiences and the benefits for niether the liege, nor the vassal are all that exciting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There\u2019s an unspoken implication in the title itself that the notary would act as a sort of harpy who would destroy the city status and reputation of either party but there\u2019s nothing explicit indicating that or empowering them in some kind of official or supernatural capacity like Carthian Laws have. </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I've forgotten to write up a Contractor merit, the Notary analogue. It'll allow you to draft Contracts. Fluff wise it'll be more accessible. Any Company member can (and is encouraged to) take the Contractor merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think your loan portion should be retooled. Loans usually involve borrowing something (possibly offering up collateral) and then paying the loan back in full with interest. With the way you have it written it basically looks like the client becomes a servant to the contractor with their payment for services being whatever \u201cloan\u201d they ask for. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree with you. That's usually how loans work in the real world when money is involved. I sort of struggled to write them up like that, though. As more goods and services can be borrowed. The structure now is more of a work to pay off your debt, which I though could work well. The second option was to represent how loans usually work, the client sacrificing a dot of a merit that can be bought immediately by the contractor. But I'm going to revisit this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you participate in multiple contracts at once? If yes, what happens if conflicting terms of different contracts arise? </div> </div> </div>Yes, you should be able to do that I suppose. I've not thought about conflicts of interests yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does physically destroying a contract void it without the other drawbacks? (Other than the loss of blood.) </div> </div> </div>I imagine that if either the contractor or the client destroys it, there is still the full range of repercussions. But when someone else destroys in that should not be the case. I'll include a line when I edit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if both parties agree to end the contract before it\u2019s expiration? </div> </div> </div>I suppose that can be part of a Contract's terms and conditions, but again: I will add in a line to make that explicit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which dice pool is used when a client uses the contractor to cast a specific ritual? It might be possible for someone to have a better dice pool than the contractor, they simply don\u2019t know the ritual in question. Alternatively hiring them to cast a specific spell may be pointless in the first place if they have to use their dice roll with nonproficiency penalties and don\u2019t have the attendant ranks. </div> </div> </div>A client uses her own dice pool. If a client wishes to learn a ritual without having any real proficiency in the necessary skills or disciplines, that's on her. Not a contractor's problem, though he might try to sell her another deal to allow her to temporarily learn the skills and disciplines required <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-25T04:25:57-07:00","id":1211355,"title":"","content":"I've edited the document, incorporating the comments. Most notably, a Contractor merit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Contractor </span></span><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022</span></span></b><br /><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisites:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Company status </span></span><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">\u2022\u2022</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effect:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> You\u2019ve been inducted into the arcane art of drawing up the agreement of a Company Contract. You can purchase Company Contract merits as the contractor party.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Drawback:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Company expects you to employ your mastery of sanguine legalise to further the ends of the covenant. Using the bounds of Company Contracts purely for personal gain, let alone to the detriment of other members, is considered a grave offense.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> <br /> And I ammended the Loan payment:<br /> <br /> </span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Payment</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: After the loan-term has come to an end, the client offers up any </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>four</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> dot combination of his Allies, Contact, Feeding grounds, Herd, Resources, Retainer, Safe place and Staff merits, for the contractor to use for an equal period of time. The client loses access to these dots. When the arrangement ends, the contractor regains control over his assets. Sanctity of merits does not apply to the contractor\u2019s temporary dots, nor does it apply to the client\u2019s offered up dots, for the repayment-period.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Alternatively, for the duration of the agreement, the client gains the Tasked condition. The task involved is specified by the contractor. The client counts as either the contractor\u2019s temporary five dot Retainer or a his temporary five dot Allies merit.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}